<App layout="vertical-sticky" name="Wrapping React components for XMLUI">
  <AppHeader>
    <Text fontWeight="bold">
      Wrapping React components for XMLUI
    </Text>
    <SpaceFiller />
    <Select
      width="120px"
      initialValue="xmlui"
      onDidChange="{ (newTheme) => setTheme(newTheme) }"
    >
      <Option value="xmlui" label="default"/>
      <Option value="earthtone" label="earthtone"/>
    </Select>
    <ToneSwitch />
    <Icon
      name="cog"
      tooltip="Inspector"
      width="20px"
      height="20px"
      onClick="inspectorDialog.open()" />
  </AppHeader>

  <NavPanel>
    <NavLink label="Home" to="/" />
    <NavGroup label="Wrapping techniques" initiallyExpanded="{true}">
      <NavLink label="wrapComponent" to="/wrap-component" />
      <NavLink label="wrapCompound" to="/wrap-compound" />
    </NavGroup>
    <NavGroup label="Level 1: Basic wrapping" initiallyExpanded="{true}">
      <NavLink label="Prop forwarding" to="/slider-vs-sliderw" />
      <NavLink label="Free tracing" to="/free-tracing" />
    </NavGroup>
    <NavGroup label="Level 2: Enrichment" initiallyExpanded="{true}">
      <NavLink label="File objects" to="/file-objects" />
      <NavLink label="BigCalendar" to="/bigcalendar" />
    </NavGroup>
    <NavGroup label="Level 3: Theming" initiallyExpanded="{true}">
      <NavLink label="Gauge (SCSS)" to="/gauge-theme" />
      <NavLink label="Calendar (runtime)" to="/calendar-theme" />
    </NavGroup>
    <NavGroup label="Level 4: Ecosystem" initiallyExpanded="{true}">
      <NavLink label="ECharts" to="/echarts" />
      <NavLink label="Tiptap" to="/tiptap" />
      <NavLink label="Extension packaging" to="/extension-packaging" />
    </NavGroup>
  </NavPanel>

  <Pages>

    <Page url="/">
      <VStack padding="{responsive('0.75rem', '2rem')}" gap="1rem">

        <H1>
          Wrapping React components for XMLUI
        </H1>

        <Markdown>
          <![CDATA[
XMLUI ships with a solid set of core components that cover basic needs. But the React ecosystem offers thousands more: charting libraries, rich-text editors, gauges, calendars, mapping tools, visualization frameworks. The [`wrapComponent`](/wrap-component) and [`wrapCompound`](/wrap-compound) functions make all of them available to XMLUI users as extension components that work exactly like core components: declarative, composable, AI-friendly, debuggable, automatable.

## Level 1: Basic wrapping

Call [`wrapComponent`](/wrap-component) or [`wrapCompound`](/wrap-compound) with a React component and minimal config. You get three things for free:

**[Prop forwarding](/slider-vs-sliderw).** All props flow through by default — you document them when you're ready, not because the component breaks without it. When the underlying library upgrades and adds new props, they're immediately available to XMLUI users.

**[Automatic tracing](/free-tracing).** Wrapped components emit semantic trace events (`value:change`, `focus:change`) with no extra code. This unlocks accessibility for screenreaders, semantic traces that AIs can reason about, and regression tests generated from user journeys by [trace-tools | target=_blank](https://github.com/xmlui-org/trace-tools).

**Progressive enhancement.** No metadata required upfront — add it incrementally as the component matures. Simple components wrap in minutes; complex libraries take longer for theming and event mapping, but the wrapper config stays small.

## Level 2: Trace enrichment

Level 1's generic tracing works for any value that stringifies cleanly. But some values need special handling.

**[Built-in: File objects](/file-objects).** The generic layer recognizes common types like `File` and emits meaningful trace labels (`report.pdf` instead of `[object File]`) plus metadata that trace-tools can use to generate test code.

**[Per-component: BigCalendar](/bigcalendar).** For domain-specific events, the render component calls `onNativeEvent` with structured fields — the wrapper traces it automatically. This is the pattern for any library with its own event model.

## Level 3: Theme bridging

A wrapped component needs to respect the design system. Three strategies, depending on the library:

**[SCSS variable mapping: Gauge](/gauge-theme).** When the library uses CSS custom properties, assign XMLUI tokens to them in SCSS. Three lines. Zero runtime cost.

**[Runtime style injection: Calendar](/calendar-theme).** When the library uses class-based CSS, resolve XMLUI tokens at runtime via `useTheme()` and inject scoped styles.

**Option-level theming: [ECharts](/echarts).** When the library styles via JavaScript config objects (canvas rendering), merge XMLUI tokens directly into the option.

## Level 4: The ecosystem unlocked

**[ECharts](/echarts).** One of the most powerful charting libraries available — time series with zoom, treemaps, donuts, toolbox interactions. Canvas-rendered, with option-level theming and comprehensive native event capture.

**[Tiptap](/tiptap).** A headless rich-text editor built on ProseMirror. Every keystroke and format toggle is semantically classified into trace-friendly native events.

**[Extension packaging](/extension-packaging).** Both ship as independent UMD bundles that auto-register via a `<script>` tag. Apps include only the components they need — one command to build, one line to load.
        ]]>
        </Markdown>

      </VStack>
    </Page>

    <Page url="/wrap-component">
      <WrapComponentPage />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/wrap-compound">
      <WrapCompoundPage />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/slider-vs-sliderw">
      <SliderVsSliderW />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/free-tracing">
      <FreeTracing />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/file-objects">
      <FileObjectTracing />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/bigcalendar">
      <BigCalendarTracing />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/gauge-theme">
      <GaugeThemeBridge />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/calendar-theme">
      <CalendarThemeBridge />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/echarts">
      <EChartsPage />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/tiptap">
      <TiptapPage />
    </Page>

    <Page url="/extension-packaging">
      <ExtensionPackaging />
    </Page>

  </Pages>

  <ModalDialog
    id="inspectorDialog"
    title="XMLUI Inspector"
    minWidth="95vw"
    minHeight="95vh">
    <IFrame src="xs-diff.html" width="100%" height="90vh" />
  </ModalDialog>
</App>